        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کھڑکی (khiṛkī) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from khaṭakkikā, \"side door\" (CDIAL 3770). The Sanskrit word is known only from the old word-lists."
            }
